Once the bet type and format are set, users input the odds for each selection in sequence. The first selection field accepts the odds for the opening leg, while the second field captures the odds for the closing leg of the double bet. Stake entry follows odds input, with the calculator accepting values in pounds and optional pence. The tool processes the calculation instantly upon completion of the final input field, displaying total return and profit figures without requiring a separate submit action.
Advanced options within the calculator handle special betting scenarios. The each way toggle activates dual calculation mode, computing both win and place returns based on the place terms specified for the event. Rule 4 deduction fields allow percentage adjustments when non-runners affect market odds in horse racing. Dead heat options split stakes between tied selections, recalculating returns according to the number of winners. These features ensure the Bet calculator provides accurate figures across all standard and exceptional betting situations encountered in GB markets.
The calculation steps follow this sequence:
